(Q1 \(Dean\): "Why not use a standard single model like VGG-16 or AlexNet?") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7.6 Tf
8.7399999999999984 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 593.5750393700786844 Td
(Answer: VGG-16 has 138M parameters \(susceptible to catastrophic overfitting on dermoscopy datasets\) and lacks residual skip connections or compound) Tj
T* (scaling. Multi-model ensembling provides orthogonal decision boundaries that capture both macro patterns and micro-vascular networks.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 562.1104724409449318 Td
(Q2 \(Dean\): "How does the system handle severe class imbalance in HAM10000?") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7.6 Tf
8.7399999999999984 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 550.7718897637795408 Td
(Answer: HAM10000 has 6,705 nevi but only 115 vascular lesions. We implemented Class-Balanced Focal Loss FL\(p_t\) = -alpha_t * \(1 - p_t\)^gamma *) Tj
T* (log\(p_t\) with gamma=2.0 and inverse-frequency class weighting, preventing the majority class from biasing gradient updates.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 519.3073228346456744 Td
(Q3 \(Dean\): "What guarantees that the model has not memorized training backgrounds?") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 7.6 Tf
8.7399999999999984 TL
0.278 0.333 0.412 rg
39.6850393700787407 507.9687401574803403 Td
(Answer: Validated via Grad-CAM gradient backpropagation: attribution heatmaps verify that layer4[-1] filters activate exclusively on intra-lesional pigment) Tj
T* (networks, with zero activation on peripheral skin markers or calibration scales.) Tj
